I am standing on the platform.
I am waiting for the U-Bahn.
A man comes up to me.
He has a city map in his hand.
He is looking for something.
"Excuse me," the man says.
"Yes, please?" I answer.
"I am looking for the Pergamon Museum," he says.
He shows me the city map.
"How do I get to the museum?" he asks.
I smile and point to the map.
"That is quite simple," I say.
"You take the next U-Bahn," I explain.
"You ride for three stops."
"Then you get out."
"The museum is right at the station."
The man is happy.
"Thank you very much for your help!" he says.
"You're welcome," I answer.
His U-Bahn arrives and he gets in.
